 # Chunk Mesh Creation
 
-Also called: Chunk Face Culling and Mesh Assembly
+Also called: Chunk Mesh Builder, Chunk-based Marching Cubes-like Mesh Generation
 
 ## Overview
-Chunk Mesh Creation generates the final visible geometry for a voxel chunk by identifying exposed block faces and assembling them into a single draw call. It solves the problem of rendering only the surfaces of a voxel chunk that are not occluded by adjacent blocks or neighboring chunks, thereby reducing overdraw and triangle count. It differs from its parent [Voxel Face Mesh Generation](4212-voxel-face-mesh-generation.md), which produces individual quads, by handling the spatial culling logic across chunk boundaries and combining multiple face meshes into one unified mesh structure.
+Chunk Mesh Creation generates the final visible geometry for a voxel chunk by identifying exposed block faces and assembling them into a single mesh [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering only the surfaces of a voxel chunk that are not occluded by adjacent blocks or neighboring chunks, thereby reducing overdraw and triangle count [S2, unofficial]. It differs from its parent [Voxel Face Mesh Generation](4212-voxel-face-mesh-generation.md), which produces individual quads, by handling the spatial culling logic across chunk boundaries and combining multiple face meshes into one unified mesh structure [S1, unofficial].
 
